This product includes and builds upon:

- OpenIPC devourer — userspace RTL8812AU/CU/EU and RTL8733BU driver, GPL-2.0.
  Vendored at `third_party/devourer/`.
  https://github.com/OpenIPC/devourer
- libusb — USB access library, LGPL-2.1-or-later.
  Vendored at `third_party/libusb-cmake/`.
  https://github.com/libusb/libusb
- nlohmann/json v3.12.0 — MIT. Vendored as a single header at
  `third_party/nlohmann/json.hpp`.
  https://github.com/nlohmann/json
  Used by the I/O layer (`io/`) only; the portable wire core (`core/`) is
  dependency-free by design.

Third-party formats reused:

- Realtek rtl88x2eu/cu driver — the `PHY_REG_PG.txt` per-rate TX-power table
  row format, reused as the per-MCS power data structure (PROTOCOL.md §10).

The broadcast injection-link approach that waybeam-link builds on was
established by the OpenIPC and wfb-ng projects.

  https://github.com/OpenIPC
  https://github.com/svpcom/wfb-ng
